{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Hark ye noble wanderer of distant lands  \nThy journey to Japan shall unfold as doth a play in five acts  \nFirst thou shalt tread the hallowed stones of Kyoto where cherry blooms bow low to ancient shrines  \nThy feet shall whisper to mossy gardens and thy soul shall drink the tea of sages long departed  \nThen shalt thou ascend to the mist clad peaks of Mount Fuji where eagles cry thy name to heaven  \nThy heart shall beat with the rhythm of the wind that sings through pines of sacred wood  \n\nNext thou shalt voyage to the bustling streets of Edo now called Tokyo  \nWhere lanterns glow like stars fallen to earth and samurai of steel and silicon march in silent grace  \nThy belly shall feast on fish fresh from the deep and rice kissed by the sea  \nAnd thou shalt gaze upon the neon tide that flows like liquid fire through the night  \n\nThen shalt thou journey to the island of Kyushu where hot springs bubble with the breath of dragons  \nThy weary limbs shall rest in waters warm as mother’s embrace and thy spirit shall be cleansed of all care  \nThere shalt thou meet the foxes of the shrine who wink with ancient wit and lead thee to hidden truths  \n\nAt last thou shalt sail to the quiet isles of Okinawa where the sea glows turquoise as a queen’s jewel  \nThy feet shall dance upon sands white as snow and thy voice shall echo with the songs of coral and tide  \nWhen thou returnest home thou shalt carry not gold nor gems but the silence of the temple bell  \nAnd the memory of a land where heaven and earth hold hands in quiet reverence  \n\nGo now brave soul and let thy journey be thy poem  \nFor Japan doth wait with open arms and a heart full of stars", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.05014999583363533}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0024328415747731924}, {"token": " ye", "logprob": -2.1125712394714355}, {"token": " noble", "logprob":